ound this pretty decent of PvP when  trying to push forward and get people  out of cover but only for short bursts  you can't just stand out in the open and  tank the day so that you can now the  bulwark shield is the traditional shield  that we used to full body cover high  defence but you can only use the sidearm  while it's out so this was just a  rundown of what we were able to test at  the event as I said on a number of  occasions depending on the sort of hard  caps a lot of these skills however  really could make or break the situation  that they'd be useful I still have hours  of footage from the event that I haven't  shown in this past few videos so had a  few more videos coming up soon at this  stage you've probably seen a number of  videos from other players who have flown  out to Red Storm and massive so what do  you think so far are you looking forward  to the division 2 after this hands-on  experience from so much more hype for  the game than it was before I had so  many concerns around the game being  oversimplified we're just generally  losing the feel of the game that have  been enjoying for the last few years but  this certainly wasn't the case if you  love the division 1 you won't be  disappointed do I think it would be  completely void of bugs and balancing  issues from day one god no these games  are far too complicated to expect there  in order to achieve true balance within  the game you need to remove all build  diversity and in doing that it would no  longer be the division I'm expecting  some teething issues for sure but for  now I need to make sure I have all of  these shields completed I want my damn  backpack teddy bear Cheers  Oh  detecting additional hostile contacts  you
 

